But remember this in your analysis.  Material is ALWAYS copyrighted, and should
be assumed copyrighted unless:
	a) it was published carelessly years ago in such a way as to lose
		copyright, or it has passed into folklore.
	b) it contains an explicit (not implicit) notice from the copyright
		holder stating that the copyright was deliberately
		abandoned, and/or that the work was placed by its owner
		into the public domain.
	c) The work can't be copyrighted -- it's very short, or is just
		a set of facts, etc.

