remove "abp.erotica", they best be prepared to remove "abp.misc" and other
groups that share the same "offense".  They also seem to turn a deaf ear to
other groups in the so called "mainstream" of USENET that have the same
problem.

There seems to be something in our society about "pictures" that causes
people to sit up and take notice.  When the material is "sounds" or "words"
there seems to be a bit less concern.  (Although "words" used to be as hot
