Where we seem to be missing each other is whether all sites on the USENET
are responsible for what is posted by some "violators".  If it is the case
that all sites are responsible for any copyright violations and this were to
be rigorously enforced, I can see that USENET, as we know it, would place
the owners of USENET sites at risk.  This includes ALL newsgroups, not just
the binary (or "SEX") ones.

So are all sites responsible for the action of a single person?  Or is the
poster and/or originating site alone responsible?

I assume the above questions and my questions from previous article must be
valid and must not have easy answers, for no one has suggested any.  So I'm
still left with my other USENET dilemmas:

        * The only reason why dropping some groups at some sites appears to
          "solve" the problem is because other major sites have refused to
          drop the groups.  This is a very short term, selfish solution.

        * If all sites drop abp.* (for whatever reason) this will not stop
          the activity, it will just cause it to move to other groups.
