City Regional Library, agrees with the McGill legal opinion.  
"Library staff cannot and do not read everything we put on our
shelves," she says.  "We are neither publishing nor distributing
anything by having this newspaper in our library."

The Halifax City Regional Library subscribes to the Canadian
Library Association's Statement on Intellectual Freedom, which
states, "It is the responsibility of libraries to guarantee and
facilitate access to all expressions of knowledge and intellectual
activity, including those which some elements of society may
consider to be unconventional, unpopular, or unacceptable."

