thinking of the Buchanan & Goodman records from a couple of
decades ago, using snippets of songs in their own records.  I
believe they were taken to court by record publishers, and were
able to win.  I think it was a "fair use" issue.  The same
thing probably came up in some of the "rap" songs produced
which incorporate other songs.

As a general proposition, it seems to me that "fair use" 
should encompass usage that does not result in a third party 
making a profit, and that does not represent loss of a lawful 
sale.  That is, unless the copyright owner can show that the 
person playing a MIDI file is using it to make money, or 
would otherwise have purchased a "legitimate"
copy of the song, then it should be considered fair use.

