nude.  To my knowledge no true "child porn" has been posted to the net
in the last two years (since I started downloading and viewing every
image).

Still, there is a problem, at least with the 'Net's image in this regard.
Certainly the existance of groups like
alt.binaries.pictures.erotica.children
and alt.sex.pedophile.mike-labbe do not help the issue.  There is nothing
that can be done about it, however, without substantially changing what
the 'Net is.  Certainly we could ban the alt. heirarchy and require that
all newsgroups be moderated, making the moderator legally responsible for
the content of their group, but that is a cure worse than the desease.

The best thing to do would be do declare the 'Net a common carrier, held
harmless for individual abuses.  That way if some dweeb post a nasty 
kiddie porn picture to a.b.p.e the poor Univeristy spooling news won't
