Copyright infringement in sufficient quantity is a felony criminal matter,
and no commercial intent is required to establish quantity under certain 
conditions.

There are a number of people who seem to post large quantities of material
to abpe.  I bet a few of them might have crossed that line.

Felonies frequently bring prison time as consequences.

I'm not sure I agree with the law as it stands on these issues, but it <is>
the law.  The three boxes which Americans have to change laws such as this
are, in order of intended use:

	1)	The ballot box
	2)	The jury box
	3)	The ammunition box

We have, as a society, abdicated the first box to the politicians.  The
second one is nearly gone too, and the third is under concerted attack by
the President and remainder of the administration.  Within the next few
years we'll have a vestige of #2, and the others will have disappeared.

What does that leave?  Comply with the law or face the consequence,
whether you believe it is a just law or not.  OR, stand up and <TAKE THE
CONSEQUENCE FOR YOUR CIVIL DISOBEDIENCE>.

That's not what happens in these groups is it?  Instead you have sniveling,
whining people posting from aliased or forged accounts so <they> don't end 
up held accountable for the theft, while exposing the rest of us to the wrath 
of the legal system.  Its like pointing a gun in the air and shooting, and 
then saying "I'm not responsible for where the bullet lands, even if it 
kills someone randomly."  NOT.

If you think I <enjoy> this you're nuts.  However, I recognize that it is
the way things are, and refuse to put my head in the sand.  Its too 
dangerous in today's society to do so.

Again - we can either police this ourselves, which might even mean nailing 
a few infringers as an example (that would quickly stop the others, I'm
willing to bet) or we can take a "head firmly between legs" attitude and 
end up with a few dozen to a few hundred machines seized, billion-dollar 
lawsuits against major net sites, and <lots> of folks in prison.

Not to mention the right-wing fundamentalists who are all over the net
no matter what we do because people like to look at "dirty pictures".

I choose the first path given the options.  The Fundies I will deal with
on my own terms.  The law is a tougher problem -- I don't have a David 
Koresh complex.

