IP providers might well attain common carrier status, if they wish to apply
for it and the FCC decides to grant it.

Services like Compuserve will never wish it when it comes to the BB/Forum
side of their business.

A common carrier can not refuse traffic, except under well defined,
universal rules.

Compuserve and other companies want to SELL the "best" information, not
all information.  They feel the market is in providing people with a value
added, selecting from the infoglut.

They are not wrong in that either, there is a market for that, though there
is also a market for wide open flow.

However, the truth is that we are talking about common *carriers* while USENET
looks much more like publishing than carriage, though my view is that it is
the poster who does the publishing, and sites only do redistribution at the
command of the poster.

Common carriers are regulated.  Their fees must be approved by the government.
They are not responsible for what they carry, though they can be ordered not
to carry it by the government.
