groups <and profit from the additional business they bring me> while ignoring
the fact that I <know> that the primary content in the group is ripped off 
is setting the company up for a monstrous problem, and fast.  No thanks.

Let's take an example from the other side of life.  Drug laws.  If you own a
house and your tenants are dealing drugs, your success in preventing the
forfeiture of that house is going to rest <squarely> on whether or not you
know about the drug dealing and what, if anything, you do about it once
you because aware of it.

If you can demonstrate that you <do not> know about it, and in fact took
reasonable precautions against it (ie: credit check, you checked the
criminal records bureau, had a strong policy against it in the lease, etc)
then you probably won't lose the house.

If on the other hand you give the tenants the keys and say "have fun" you
might be in trouble.  If you then <ignore the problem> when the neighbors 
call you to complain that there is a 30-person queue outside of the door, 
and the neighbors are convinced the tenants are dealing crack, you're going 
to lose.  Every time.  And, in fact, people <do> lose on this basis with
some frequency.

If you're reading this thread then you've been told that the abps and abpe 
